---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import '../../../../lib/equipment/07-02/style.css';
import verification from '../../../../../public/equipment/07-02/verification.json';
const base='/equipment/07-02/';
const manual='https://knowledge1.thermofisher.com/@api/deki/files/37464/50144132-EN_-_Rev_A_-_Heracell_Vios_160i_and_250i_CO2_Incubators_Operating_Manual.pdf?revision=1#page=';
const brochure='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LED/brochures/Heracell-VIOS-CO2-Incubator-BRCO2VIOSNA-EN.pdf#page=';
const graph='https://knowledge1.thermofisher.com/Lab_Equipment/CO2_Incubators/Thermo_Scientific_Heraeus_CO2_Incubators/Thermo_Scientific_Heraeus_Operator_Manuals/Recovery_and_Gas_Consumption_Graphs';
const photos='https://newlifescientific.com/products/thermo-scientific-heracell-vios-160i-stainless-steel-co2-incubator-with-cart-1';
const cdn='https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0064/4268/0410/files/';
const views=[
  ['front','Cabinet and controller','The front elevation establishes the left handle, dark fascia and right-hand touchscreen. The side photographs locate the front seam and projecting rear enclosure.','59323888_c52968f8-3f62-4055-96dd-c6581bcab575.jpg','Front photograph','59323894_2146a7b3-07cb-4dec-919e-55aab2082d50.jpg','Side elevations'],
  ['chamber','Sample-loading area','The open view locates the glass latch, right-hand hinges, perforated shelf inserts and rear air duct. The photographed shelf arrangement differs from the three installed levels in this model.','59323891_26076063-43e5-4bed-9994-0338da438b49.jpg','Chamber photograph','59323890_bd3ebbf2-9072-4ddd-8c4b-163cdb39058c.jpg','Glass door closed'],
  ['rear','Service connections','The rear view places the plugged chamber port beside the service enclosure. The service photograph shows the vertical order of the data, alarm and power connections. Port offsets are estimated.','59323896_b6d08d4e-299e-4e7c-b133-e2a3c23def72.jpg','Rear and nameplate','59323895_0f8f00ab-86bf-4c32-87fd-0147d72c1282.jpg','Connector detail']
];
const specs=[
  ['Cabinet, W × H × D','637 × 905 × 790 mm','Nominal manual envelope used for scale. The North American brochure gives 637 × 900 × 880 mm. The reason for the depth difference is undocumented.','Manual pp. 2-2, 11-2',manual+26],
  ['Chamber, W × H × D','470 × 607 × 576 mm','Interior bounds. Nominal capacity is 165 L.','Manual p. 11-2',manual+158],
  ['Standard shelves','3 × 423 × 465 mm (count × W × D)','10 kg per shelf, 30 kg total rated load. This experiment tracks one reserved position per shelf.','Brochure p. 15',brochure+15],
  ['Shelf rails / access port','42 mm rail pitch / Ø42 mm port','Manual mounting interval and rear opening. Shelf elevations, hinge offsets, glass thickness and hole pattern are reconstructed.','Manual pp. 3-21–3-22',manual+51],
  ['Temperature control','Room + 3 to 55 °C','Hardware range for a single instrument. Model uses 25–45 °C at fixed 22 °C ambient.','Manual p. 11-2',manual+158],
  ['CO₂ control','1–20 vol %','Brochure active range. Model uses 1–15 vol %. Installed TC180 senses CO₂.','Brochure pp. 15–16',brochure+15],
  ['Glass-door switch','Open / closed','Opening the glass door interrupts gas delivery and heating. Animation angles are illustrative.','Manual p. 3-10',manual+40],
  ['Documented test','30 s opening','Separate TC CO₂ and centre-temperature responses. Sensor traces continue through recovery after closure.','Recovery graphs pp. 2, 5',graph]
];
const fields=[['temp_C','Temperature setpoint (°C)',37,25,45,.1],['co2_pct','CO₂ setpoint (vol %)',5,1,15,.1],['duration_s','Run duration (s)',1200,120,3600,1],['start_s','Door visit begins (s)',270,0,3599,1],['open_s','Visit duration (s)',30,1,120,1]];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Incubator laboratory" subtitle="" description="Replay a measured CO₂ excursion in a 3D HERAcell VIOS 160i and trace the chamber conditions each sample experienced.">
<article class="equipment vios">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/07-02/">← Equipment 07-02</a><a href="#vios-references">Illustrated references</a><a href="#vios-verification">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="v-mast"><div><p class="eyeline">Thermo Scientific · Equipment 07-02</p><h2>Heracell VIOS 160i</h2></div><p>Replay a 30-second door opening. Which samples were in the chamber when the CO₂ concentration fell?</p></header>
<div class="v-desk">
<section class="v-instrument" aria-label="Instrument viewer">
  <div class="v-bar"><strong>Instrument</strong><span id="vios-model-msg" role="status">Loading geometry…</span></div>
  <div id="vios-view" aria-label="3D incubator. Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom."><img id="vios-poster" src={base+'geometry/chamber.webp'} alt="Open chamber of the incubator reconstruction" /></div>
  <div class="v-tools">{[['whole','Reset view'],['chamber','Chamber'],['controller','Controller'],['rear','Rear']].map(([key,text])=><button data-camera={key} disabled>{text}</button>)}</div>
  <div class="v-tools"><button id="vios-outer">Close outer door</button><button id="vios-glass">Open glass door</button><button id="vios-bench" disabled>Return to setup</button></div>
  <p class="minor">Drag to orbit. Pinch or scroll to zoom. In setup, open the glass door to inspect the shelves. During a replay the clock positions both doors.</p>
</section>
<section class="v-setup" aria-label="Experiment setup">
  <div class="v-bar"><strong>Experiment</strong><span>51030285 · TC180</span></div>
  <label class="v-field">Source<select id="vios-mode"><option value="tc">Recorded CO₂ excursion</option><option value="temperature">Recorded temperature excursion</option><option value="model">Simulated door visit</option><option value="imported">Import chamber logger CSV</option></select></label>
  <div id="vios-log-input" hidden><label class="v-field">Logger file<input id="vios-logger" type="file" accept=".csv,text/csv"/></label><a href={base+'example-logger.csv'} download>Example CSV (synthetic, 300 s)</a></div>
  <fieldset id="vios-model-settings" hidden><legend>Chamber model</legend><div class="v-fields">{fields.map(([id,label,value,min,max,step])=><label class="v-field">{label}<input id={'vios-'+id} type="number" {value} {min} {max} {step}/></label>)}
  <label class="v-field">Door visit<select id="vios-access"><option value="glass">Open both doors</option><option value="outer">Open outer door only</option></select></label></div><label><input id="vios-connected" type="checkbox" checked/> CO₂ supply connected</label></fieldset>
  <h3>Shelf reservations</h3><p class="minor">Enter and leave times use seconds from the start of this trace. Shelf 1 is the lowest.</p>
  <div class="scroll"><table class="v-inputs"><thead><tr><th>Sample ID</th><th>Shelf</th><th>Enter (s)</th><th>Leave (s)</th><th><span class="sr">Actions</span></th></tr></thead><tbody id="vios-schedules"></tbody></table></div>
  <div class="v-tools"><button id="vios-add">Add sample</button><button id="vios-reset">Restore example</button></div>
  <details><summary>Import a sample map</summary><label class="v-field">Reservations JSON<input id="vios-manifest" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label><a href={base+'example-samples.json'} download>Example sample map</a></details>
  <button id="vios-run" class="v-primary" disabled>Run experiment</button><p id="vios-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading the manufacturer trace…</p>
</section></div>
<section class="v-record"><div class="v-bar"><strong>Chamber record</strong><span id="vios-source"></span></div>
  <dl class="v-values">{[['Clock','clock'],['Chamber temperature','temp'],['Chamber CO₂','co2'],['Door state','door-state'],['Occupancy','occupants']].map(([label,id])=><div><dt>{label}</dt><dd id={'vios-'+id}>—</dd></div>)}</dl>
  <div class="v-chart"><label class="v-field">Plotted channel<select id="vios-channel" aria-label="Plotted channel"></select></label><svg id="vios-chart" role="img" aria-label="Chamber readings against elapsed seconds, with glass-door interval shaded and shelf occupancy bars beneath"></svg></div>
  <div class="v-clock"><button id="vios-play" disabled>Play trace</button><label>Inspect time (s)<input id="vios-timeline" aria-label="Inspect elapsed time in seconds" type="range" min="0" max="1800" value="0" step="1" disabled/></label></div>
  <p class="minor">The shaded band marks the glass-door interval. Shelf bars show the reservations. Playback runs at 30×. <span id="vios-event-note"></span>.</p>
  <div id="vios-result" hidden><h3>Sample exposure</h3><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Sample</th><th>Shelf</th><th>Window (s)</th><th>Glass open (s)</th><th id="vios-metric-head">Minimum</th><th id="vios-mean-head">Mean</th><th id="vios-below-head">Below threshold (s)</th></tr></thead><tbody id="vios-metrics"></tbody></table></div></div>
  <div class="v-tools"><button id="vios-json" disabled>Export histories (JSON)</button><button id="vios-csv" disabled>Export sample readings (CSV)</button><a href={base+'output-schema.json'}>Output schema</a><a href={base+'example-result.json'}>Example result</a></div>
</section>
<section id="vios-references"><h2>Illustrated reference sheet</h2><p>The 120 V North American unit shown here has a white cabinet, one stainless-steel chamber, an unsegmented glass door, three shelf inserts and a thermal-conductivity CO₂ sensor. The original model renderings are paired with photographs of a unit whose nameplate identifies catalog 51030285 and a January 2019 manufacture date. The optional roller cart in the photographs is excluded. <a href={photos}>New Life Scientific photo set</a> · <a href={brochure+16}>Manufacturer ordering matrix, p. 16</a>.</p>
  <div class="v-plates">{views.map(([file,title,desc,img,label,img2,label2])=><figure><a href={base+'geometry/'+file+'.webp'}><img loading="lazy" src={base+'geometry/'+file+'.webp'} alt={'Original labeled model render: '+title}/></a><figcaption><strong>{title}</strong>{desc} <a href={cdn+img}>{label}</a> · <a href={cdn+img2}>{label2}</a>.</figcaption></figure>)}</div>
  <p><a href={base+'geometry/heracell-vios-160i.glb'} download>Download instrument GLB</a> · <a href={base+'geometry/build_model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={base+'geometry/model-notes.md'}>Geometry checks and rendering notes</a> · <a href={cdn+'59323889_f859e289-620c-40d0-80d3-bc232f86d38f.jpg'}>Photographed controller</a> · <a href="https://www.hajim.rochester.edu/bme/sites/hcic/about/index.html">University of Rochester installation</a>.</p>
  <h3>Specifications and reconstruction limits</h3><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th><th>Use in this model</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{specs.map(([item,val,meaning,name,url])=><tr><th>{item}</th><td>{val}</td><td>{meaning}</td><td><a href={url}>{name}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h2>How the experiment works</h2>
  <h3>Recorded excursions</h3><p>Thermo Scientific’s 2018 recovery report plots a TC180 CO₂ response on p. 5 and a chamber-centre temperature response on p. 2. Each run has its own clock. The simulator interpolates digitized points on the selected curve and leaves the other channel empty. The report specifies a 30-second opening. The position of that interval on each clock is inferred from the first visible departure. Recovery continues after the door closes. <a href={graph}>Manufacturer graphs</a> · <a href={base+'records/evidence.md'}>Axis calibration and digitization uncertainty</a>.</p>
  <h3>Adjustable chamber model</h3><p>During a glass-door visit the one-zone model exchanges heat and gas with room air at 22 °C and 0.04 vol % CO₂. During closure it relaxes toward the selected setpoints. For either channel, X(t + Δt) = X<sub>target</sub> + (X(t) − X<sub>target</sub>) 2<sup>−Δt/h</sup>. Open/closed half-times h are 30/65 s for temperature and 15/75 s for CO₂. These are illustrative transport and recovery parameters. Opening only the outer door leaves the model chamber sealed. A disconnected virtual gas supply blocks model startup. The recorded replays remain independent of these settings. <a href={base+'solver.mjs'}>Numerical source</a>.</p>
  <h3>Sample and logger contract</h3><p>Sample IDs and shelf numbers label retrospective occupancy intervals [enter, leave). The loader accepts up to 12 reservations on three shelves and checks for time conflicts in each reserved slot. The setup preview shows the vessels present at time zero. Schedule boundaries describe custody and do not add extra unrecorded door events. Chamber readings describe ambient exposure. They do not establish specimen temperature, gas exchange in a sealed dish, growth or viability.</p>
  <p>Logger CSV uses the header <code>time_s,temp_C,co2_pct,glass_open</code>. Time begins at zero and increases to at most 7,200 s. Gaps over 120 s are rejected. Provide one or both continuous channels within 0–60 °C and 0–20 vol % CO₂, leaving unused columns blank. The glass switch is 0 or 1 and holds until its next timestamp. The outer-door pose for an imported single-switch record follows the glass switch.</p>
  <p>Each output carries the source, units, clock, device and sample IDs, shelf, parent and new revisions, prior history, and optional contact IDs. Exposure clipping inserts a boundary value by linear interpolation. The leave-time value closes the integration interval. Trapezoidal time-weighted means and exact linear threshold crossings use chamber-air thresholds of 4.5 vol % and 36.5 °C as descriptive markers. The JSON schema and example define the downstream environmental-history handoff. <a href={base+'example-samples.json'}>Sample map</a> · <a href={base+'output-schema.json'}>Handoff schema</a>.</p></section>
<section id="vios-verification"><h2>Verification</h2><p>Interval arithmetic and half-life fixtures were specified before implementation. Graph checks compare the extracted values with independent visual readings of the same published plots. They verify the replay transcription. Predictive accuracy of the adjustable model has not been experimentally established.</p>
  <div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Unit</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody>{verification.map(r=><tr><td>{r.test}</td><td>{r.expected}</td><td>{Number(r.actual.toFixed(3))}</td><td>{r.unit}</td><td>{r.tolerance}</td><td>{r.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p><a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification results (JSON)</a> · <a href={base+'records/tc180-co2.csv'}>Digitized TC trace</a> · <a href={base+'records/center-temperature.csv'}>Digitized temperature trace</a>.</p>
</section></article></Layout>
<script>
import {init} from '../../../../lib/equipment/07-02/client.js';
init().catch(error=>{const status=document.getElementById('vios-status');if(status)status.textContent='Experiment unavailable. '+error.message;});
</script>
